            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_1a86f182">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="persName_id4d0597cd">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
            </contributor>
            <history xml:id="history_id91147d9b">
               <p xml:id="idm60">The collection of six trios, which is only listed in the Breitkopf auction catalogue of 1836, has presumably not survived. The catalogue does not provide any detailed information on the collection. It should be noted that it does not occur in the earlier sales catalogues but the collection might be among the works mentioned in Scheibe’s autobiography of 1739 (see Mattheson, <rend xml:id="idm61" fontstyle="italic">Grundlage</rend>, 1740; SchW C5:001).</p>
            </history>
